    <statement><p>Consider the four functions graphed in the figure below, and assume the equations for <em> A</em>, <em> B</em>, <em> C</em>, and <em> D</em>, can all be written in the form <m>y=ab^t</m>.</p>
<p>Which two functions have the same value for <m>a</m>?
<var form="popup">
<li>
<p>?</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>AC</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>AD</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>CD</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>BC</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>BD</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>AB</p>
</li>
</var></p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/sec-exp-functions-9-5-image-1.png" width="66%"/>
<p>(click on image to enlarge)</p>
</statement>
    <solution><alert>  SOLUTION </alert>



Since <m>y=a</m> when <m>t=0</m> in <m>y=ab^t</m>, <m>a</m> is the <m>y</m>-intercept.  Thus, the two functions with the same <em> y</em>-intercept, are B and D.



</solution>
